    /// <p>The QColor constructor creates the color based on RGB values. To create a QColor based on either HSV or CMYK values, use the <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qcolor.html#toHsv" translate="no">toHsv</a>() and <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qcolor.html#toCmyk" translate="no">toCmyk</a>() functions respectively. These functions return a copy of the color using the desired format. In addition the static <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qcolor.html#fromRgb" translate="no">fromRgb</a>(), <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qcolor.html#fromHsv" translate="no">fromHsv</a>() and <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qcolor.html#fromCmyk" translate="no">fromCmyk</a>() functions create colors from the specified values. Alternatively, a color can be converted to any of the three formats using the <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qcolor.html#convertTo" translate="no">convertTo</a>() function (returning a copy of the color in the desired format), or any of the <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qcolor.html#setRgb" translate="no">setRgb</a>(), <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qcolor.html#setHsv" translate="no">setHsv</a>() and <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qcolor.html#setCmyk" translate="no">setCmyk</a>() functions altering <i>this</i> color's format. The <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qcolor.html#spec" translate="no">spec</a>() function tells how the color was specified.</p>
