    /// <p>QRasterWindow is a <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qwindow.html" translate="no">QWindow</a> with a raster-based, non-OpenGL surface. On top of the functionality offered by <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qwindow.html" translate="no">QWindow</a>, QRasterWindow adds a virtual <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qpaintdevicewindow.html#paintEvent" translate="no">paintEvent</a>() function and the possibility to open a <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qpainter.html" translate="no">QPainter</a> on itself. The underlying paint engine will be the raster one, meaning that all drawing will happen on the CPU. For performing accelerated, OpenGL-based drawing, use <a href="http://doc.qt.io/qt-5/qopenglwindow.html" translate="no">QOpenGLWindow</a> instead.</p>
